  "rationale": "ConfigurationTyped.progress has only the framed typed premise and returns finished or an existential framed patternOperation successor under classes.erase. The prose erasure and transition notation come from configuration/typing units. In particular, empty code is handled by exit, whereas no-frame terminal is finished. This is operational progress, with no added success premise. Rooted-foundation review: the structural invariants now require explicit rootedness (including pending values) plus unique/compatible ownership. Allocation bounds remain solely for freshness; no safety proof assumes edge-age order or global DAG structure. Changed proof selections retain their public statement unless this unit explicitly defines the revised invariant or example. Given/Shared root transport and path reasoning were reviewed by their implementing agents, with fresh review of root-owned unpacking, GC, frame rerooting, class retention and the refill example. Earlier syntax and runtime rules are unchanged. The widened invariant domain is covered by recompilation of all earlier safety proofs and concrete shared-cycle/nonmonotonic-ID regressions, not by a claim that constructors can generate cycles.",
